    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d64">

                <pb facs="0097" n="89" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg89"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/1407: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-02-11T11:00:00+00:00">February 11, 1939—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 11—8:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>206. From Myron Taylor. The organizations here which are deeply concerned with
                    the improvement of prospects for colonization in Brazil have urged me to
                    telegraph you requesting that the President or the Secretary urge upon Senhor
                        Aranha,<anchor n="35" xml:id="d64-f1"/> now in Washington, that Brazil take
                    prompt and decisive action in the premises. It would be useful for us here if
                    you could wire me such request of Aranha has been made. [Myron Taylor.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d64-f1" n="35" xml:id="d64-f1-content">
                <p>Oswaldo Aranha, Brazilian Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
